{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1256989-fae-touched-and-glamour","id":1256989,"title":"Fae Touched and Glamour","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-09-24T11:05:00-07:00","id":1256989,"title":"Fae Touched and Glamour","content":"So, I have a player in a new chronicle using Changeling 2nd ed.<br /> <br /> Everyone else is happy to be one of the Lost, but for his own reasons, he wants to play Fae Touched instead. All well and good ... until we started looking at Wyrd, Glamour, and Contracts.<br /> <br /> Fae Touched are granted a limited number of Contracts and can purchase others. Fae Touched have Wyrd 0 and cannot, as far as I am able to ascertain, may not raise this. Fae Touched may not use Loopholes for Contracts. Wyrd 0, as far as I can tell from the rules, does not grant any Glamour...<br /> <br /> ...so how are the Fae Touched able to power Contracts?<br /> <br /> I have probably just overlooked something, but I would appreciate any insight on the topic <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5435-mhicwombat","name":"MhicWombat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5435_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"45"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-24T11:12:52-07:00","id":1256992,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l